            "9"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-h01"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        "QUESTION POSÉE... ",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "9"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-h01"
        }
      ],
      "units": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u003",
      "page": "",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u003"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "当我们把目光投向一幅艺术图像（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "9"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-h01"
        },
        "）。向一种确信无疑的腔调提出的问题（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "10"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u003"
        },
        "）。向康德式腔调、若干魔法词和一种知识的地位提出的问题（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "12"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u008"
        },
        "）。形象表现性那极为古老的要求（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "15"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u014"
        },
        "）。"
      ],
      "en": [
        "Lorsque nous posons notre regard sur une image de l’art (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "9"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-h01"
        },
        "). Question posée à un ton de certitude (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "10"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u003"
        },
        "). Question posée à un ton kantien, à quelques mots magiques et au statut d’un savoir (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "12"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u008"
        },
        "). La très ancienne exigence de figurabilité (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "15"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=q#q-u014"
        },
        ")."
      ],
      "units": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u004",
      "page": "",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u004"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "1. 简单实践范围中的艺术史……",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "19"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-h01"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        "1. L’HISTOIRE DE L’ART DANS LES LIMITES DE SA SIMPLE PRATIQUE... ",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "19"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-h01"
        }
      ],
      "units": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u005",
      "page": "",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u005"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "投向一块白色墙面的目光：可见者、可读者、不可见者、视觉性、虚拟者（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "21"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u003"
        },
        "）。视觉性的要求，或道成肉身如何“打开”模仿（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "36"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u025"
        },
        "）。学科如何像提防非知一样提防理论。特殊性的错觉、精确性的错觉与“历史家的花招”（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "41"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u033"
        },
        "）。过去如何对过去形成屏障。不可或缺的发现与不可思议的丧失。",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "历史"
          ]
        },
        "与",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "艺术"
          ]
        },
        "如何前来阻碍艺术史（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "48"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u043"
        },
        "）。第一个平庸之谈：艺术已经终结……自艺术史存在以来。形而上学陷阱与实证主义陷阱（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "54"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u052"
        },
        "）。第二个平庸之谈：一切皆可见……自艺术死亡以来（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "63"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u073"
        },
        "）。"
      ],
      "en": [
        "Regard posé sur un pan de mur blanc : le visible, le lisible, l’invisible, le visuel, le virtuel (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "21"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u003"
        },
        "). L’exigence du visuel, ou comment l’incarnation « ouvre » l’imitation (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "36"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u025"
        },
        "). Où la discipline se méfie de la théorie comme du non-savoir. L’illusion de spécificité, l’illusion d’exactitude et le « coup de l’historien » (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "41"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u033"
        },
        "). Où le passé fait écran au passé. L’indispensable trouvaille et l’impensable perte. Où l’",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "histoire"
          ]
        },
        " et l’",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "art"
          ]
        },
        " viennent faire obstacle à l’histoire de l’art (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "48"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u043"
        },
        "). Première banalité : l’art est fini... depuis qu’existe l’histoire de l’art. Piège métaphysique et piège positiviste (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "54"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u052"
        },
        "). Seconde banalité : tout est visible... depuis que l’art est mort (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "63"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c1#c1-u073"
        },
        ")."
      ],
      "units": 102
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u006",
      "page": "",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u006"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "2. 作为复兴的艺术与理想之人的不朽……",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "65"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-h01"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        "2. L’ART COMME RENAISSANCE ET L’IMMORTALITÉ DE L’HOMME IDÉAL... ",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "65"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-h01"
        }
      ],
      "units": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u007",
      "page": "331–332",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u007"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "艺术如何被发明为从自身灰烬中重生，艺术史又如何随之被发明（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "67"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u003"
        },
        "）。瓦萨里《名人传》的四重合法化：对君主的服从、艺术的社会体、对起源的诉求与对目的的诉求（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "71"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u009"
        },
        "）。瓦萨里如何把艺术家们从遗忘中拯救出来，并在",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "eterna fama"
          ]
        },
        "（永恒的名声）中“重新命名”他们。艺术史作为一种次级宗教，致力于理想之人的不朽（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "77"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u020"
        },
        "）。形而上学的目的与廷臣的目的。裂隙如何在理想与实在论中被重新缝合：一种神奇记事板的操作（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "82"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u031"
        },
        "）。前三个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "rinascita"
          ]
        },
        "（复兴）、",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "imitazione"
          ]
        },
        "（模仿）、",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "idea"
          ]
        },
        "（理念）（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "89"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u042"
        },
        "）。第四个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "disegno"
          ]
        },
        "（素描／设计）。艺术如何作为统一的对象、高贵的实践与理智的知识而合法化。费德里科·祖卡里的形而上学。艺术史如何按自己的形象创造艺术（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "94"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u053"
        },
        "）。"
      ],
      "en": [
        "Où l’art fut inventé comme renaissant de ses cendres, et où l’histoire de l’art avec lui s’inventa (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "67"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u003"
        },
        "). Les quatre légitimations des ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "Vies"
          ]
        },
        " de Vasari : l’obédience au prince, le corps social de l’art, l’appel à l’origine et l’appel aux fins (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "71"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u009"
        },
        "). Où Vasari sauve les artistes de l’oubli et les « renomme » dans l’",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "eterna fama."
          ]
        },
        " L’histoire de l’art comme religion seconde, vouée à l’immortalité d’hommes idéaux (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "77"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u020"
        },
        "). Fins métaphysiques et fins courtisanes. Où la fêlure se recoud dans l’idéal et le réalisme : une opération de bloc-notes magique (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "82"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u031"
        },
        "). Les trois premiers mots magiques : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "rinascita, imitazione, idea"
          ]
        },
        " (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "89"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u042"
        },
        "). Le quatrième mot magique : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "disegno."
          ]
        },
        " Où l’art se légitime en tant qu’objet unifié, pratique noble et connaissance intellectuelle. La métaphysique de Federico Zuccari. Où l’histoire de l’art crée l’art à sa propre image (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "94"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c2#c2-u053"
        },
        ")."
      ],
      "units": 131
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u008",
      "page": "332",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u008"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "3. 单纯理性范围中的艺术史……",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "105"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-h01"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        "3. L’HISTOIRE DE L’ART DANS LES LIMITES DE SA SIMPLE RAISON... ",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "105"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-h01"
        }
      ],
      "units": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "tmat-u009",
      "page": "",
      "canonical_kind": "paragraph",
      "source_ids": [
        "tmat-u009"
      ],
      "zh": [
        "瓦萨里遗留给我们的种种目的。单纯理性，或话语如何发明其对象（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "107"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u003"
        },
        "）。瓦萨里论题的种种变形、反题时刻的浮现：艺术史所采纳的康德式腔调（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "110"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u007"
        },
        "）。欧文·帕诺夫斯基如何展开反题与批判的时刻。可见者如何获得意义。解释的暴力（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "116"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u018"
        },
        "）。从反题到综合。康德式的目的、形而上学的目的。作为魔法操作的综合（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "127"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u035"
        },
        "）。第一个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "humanisme"
          ]
        },
        "（人文主义）。知识的对象如何成为知识的形式。康德式的瓦萨里与人文主义的康德。意识的种种权力与向理想之人的回归（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "134"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u046"
        },
        "）。第二个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "iconologie"
          ]
        },
        "（图像学）。回到切萨雷·里帕。可见者、可读者、不可见者。作为先验综合的图像学内容概念。帕诺夫斯基的退却（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "145"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u066"
        },
        "）。更远、太远了：唯心主义的约束。第三个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "forme symbolique"
          ]
        },
        "（象征形式）。可感符号如何被可知者消化。功能的相关性、“功能统一体”的唯心主义（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "153"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u079"
        },
        "）。从图像到概念、从概念到图像。第四个魔法词：",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "schématisme"
          ]
        },
        "（图式论）。综合在再现中的最终统一。凝为花押字的、被简缩的、“纯粹的”图像。一门被约束于逻辑与形而上学的艺术科学（",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "160"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u092"
        },
        "）。"
      ],
      "en": [
        "Les fins que nous a léguées Vasari. La simple raison, ou comment le discours invente son objet (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "107"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u003"
        },
        "). Métamorphoses de la thèse vasarienne, émergences du moment de l’antithèse : le ton kantien adopté par l’histoire de l’art (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "110"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u007"
        },
        "). Où Erwin Panofsky développe le moment d’antithèse et de critique. Comment le visible prend sens. La violence de l’interprétation (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "116"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u018"
        },
        "). De l’antithèse à la synthèse. Fins kantiennes, fins métaphysiques. La synthèse comme opération magique (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "127"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u035"
        },
        "). Le premier mot magique : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "humanisme."
          ]
        },
        " Où l’objet du savoir devient forme du savoir. Vasari kantien et Kant humaniste. Pouvoirs de la conscience et retour à l’homme idéal (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "134"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u046"
        },
        "). Le second mot magique : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "iconologie."
          ]
        },
        " Retour à Cesare Ripa. Visible, lisible, invisible. La notion de contenu iconologique comme synthèse transcendantale. Le recul de Panofsky (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "145"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u066"
        },
        "). Plus loin, trop loin : la contrainte idéaliste. Le troisième mot magique : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "forme symbolique."
          ]
        },
        " Où le signe sensible est digéré par l’intelligible. Pertinence de la fonction, idéalisme de l’« unité de la fonction » (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "153"
          ],
          "url": "translations/book.html?id=devant-limage&chapter=c3#c3-u079"
        },
        "). De l’image au concept et du concept à l’image. Le quatrième mot magique : ",
        {
          "type": "em",
          "children": [
            "schématisme."
          ]
        },
        " Unité finale de la synthèse dans la représentation. L’image monogrammée, abrégée, « pure ». Une science de l’art contrainte à la logique et à la métaphysique (",
        {
          "type": "link",
          "children": [
            "160"
          ],
